--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8eb9d9fa0ccbe1b4cbcd2a1d889b806b, type: 3}
  m_Name: FirstDayConvo04
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Dialogue
  conversationName: FirstDayMainConversation
  lines:
  - speakerName: Randy
    line: There is no need for thanks-- just make good use of that tool, and don't
      botch any harvesting.
  - speakerName: Randy
    line: Hm? Oh yes, it takes skill to harvest materials <b>while preserving their
      quality</b>. Make sure you are <i>careful and precise</i> while extracting
      to get high quality materials..
  - speakerName: Randy
    line: Also-- make sure <b>not to drop the organs</b> and materials after you
      have harvested them, or their <b>quality will degrade</b>.
  - speakerName: Randy
    line: I trust that <i>even</i> you can do something that simple without messing
      it up, yes?
  - speakerName: Randy
    line: If you damage or drop an organ so much that its <b>quality reaches 0%</b>,
      it will be too damaged to salvage-- and <b>it will disappear</b>. So <b>be
      careful when transporting the goods.</b>
  - speakerName: Randy
    line: Also, do try to sell goods that are <b>high quality</b>, or else the customers
      will not pay a high price for them. Selling high-quality products will make
      it easier to reach quota.
  - speakerName: Randy
    line: Now, with all of that out of the way, here-- take this <b>room key</b>.
      Use that to <b>unlock the door to one of the guest rooms</b>, so that you can
      <b>enter and begin harvesting from the guest</b>.
  repeatLine:
    speakerName: Randy
    line: "You\u2019ve got the room key, the room is waiting, and the guest is...
      well, not going anywhere. Go on."
  altRepeatLine:
    speakerName: Randy
    line: "Here is the next room key. It\u2019s a little sticky. Don\u2019t worry
      about why."
